# Docker reads .dockerignore from the *build context root*, and this service is
# built with `context: ./backend`. The repo-root .dockerignore is therefore never
# consulted for this image, and its `backend/...` patterns would not match here
# anyway — paths are relative to the context.
#
# Without this file the image shipped with backend/.env in it (the live Gemini
# key), every stored dataset snapshot, every fitted model bundle, the test suite,
# and scratch/. Found in Phase 7 by looking inside a built image instead of
# assuming; see docs/phase7-results.md.

# Secrets. First, and the reason this file exists.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generated artifacts: dataset snapshots, fitted models, the job database, and
# uploads spooled for the worker. All runtime state, all mounted as a volume at
# runtime — baking a build-time copy in both leaks data and shadows the mount.
models/

# Not needed to serve, and each one is extra attack surface in the image.
tests/
scratch/

# Build noise.
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
